      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "If $g(x)$ is given by the table shown below, what are its roots?\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $20$ | $30$ | $40$ | $50$ | $60$ | $70$ | $80$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $5$ | $15$ | $25$ | $0$ | $-15$ | $-25$ | $0$ | $5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $g(x)=0.$ In the given table, we see that $g(40)=0$ and $g(70)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=40$ and $x=70.$",
